# rainbow-www — environment
#
# With NONE of these set, the dashboard runs the deterministic seeded
# simulator and says so: every API response carries `synthetic: true` and the
# page header reads "Synthetic demo". That is a valid deployment state.
#
# Set all three to make it real: signals POSTed to /api/signals are persisted,
# and the read path flips itself to live. Nothing is hardcoded — provenance is
# derived per request from whether real signals are actually present.

# --- Persistent signal store (Supabase) ---
# Apply sql/rainbow-signals.sql to the project first.
# The service role key is server-only and must never reach the client; the
# production RLS policy grants anon nothing at all.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --- Ingest auth ---
# Bearer token required by POST /api/signals, compared in constant time.
# Unset means ingest is DISABLED (503) — it fails closed, never silently
# accepting and dropping signals.
RAINBOW_INGEST_TOKEN=
